{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-af8adc80-c963-4579-8c41-e7b2c8bb403c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb9948f96253900f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-9n71jeu4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006 ([TP] Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator)\n\nTriage: full decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy spans four\naffected components, three development teams plus QE and Docs, and is estimated at L\n(6–9 sprints). The Staff Engineer Input section contains only template placeholder text —\nno overrides to apply.\n\n## Component Mapping (canonical RHAI components)\n\n| Strategy component | Canonical component | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| kagenti-operator | Agentic | Not in `.context/rhai-components.txt` verbatim; \"Agentic\" is the closest canonical component for kagenti work |\n| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | Same mapping; distinct repo/image family, kept as separate epics (different repos and work products) despite the shared canonical name |\n| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | Platform operator component-integration work; rhods-operator is the core platform operator |\n| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Direct match |\n| QE work (no owned component) | QE | E2E / disconnected-install validation |\n| Docs work (no owned component) | Documentation | Installation and enablement documentation |\n\nNew-component detection: no architecture context file exists for kagenti-operator or\nkagenti-extensions → both get the Rule 20 onboarding chain (`repo-onboarding` +\n`license-validation` parallel start → `konflux-onboarding` after repo-onboarding). There is\nno general implementation epic for either repo: the strategy explicitly excludes the\noperator's runtime capabilities (registration, discovery, sidecar injection already exist\nupstream); the work is build pipeline, platform integration, and packaging.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality (gap analysis) | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Establish opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator midstream fork | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | License validation for kagenti-operator dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Konflux onboarding for kagenti-operator container image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E005 | Determine AuthBridge sidecar variants required for TP | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E006 | Establish opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions midstream fork | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E007 | License validation for kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E008 | Konflux onboarding for AuthBridge sidecar images | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E009 | KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE entries | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | Decide dashboard integration depth for TP | Investigation | Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 | Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | Dashboard agent list UI module | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | QE test plan, E2E lifecycle and disconnected-install validation | Implementation | QE | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E015 | Resolve OTEL trace sink scope for TP | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E016 | kagenti-operator installation and image-contract documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P0 |\n\nBranch epic (conditional, attached to E001's outcome, not a main-plan node):\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E017 | Close upstream kagenti-operator functional gaps | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E002[RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 repo-onboarding kagenti-operator] --> E004[RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 Konflux kagenti-operator image]\n    E006[RHAISTRAT-8006-E006 repo-onboarding kagenti-extensions] --> E008[RHAISTRAT-8006-E008 Konflux AuthBridge images]\n    E005[RHAISTRAT-8006-E005 AuthBridge variants investigation] --> E008\n    E001[RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 upstream gap analysis] --> E009[RHAISTRAT-8006-E009 DSC component controller]\n    E009 --> E010[RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 OLM/CSV packaging]\n    E009 --> E014[RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 QE E2E and disconnected validation]\n    E010 --> E014\n    E011[RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 dashboard depth investigation] --> E013[RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 agent list UI module]\n    E012[RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 dashboard BFF plugin] --> E013\n    E015[RHAISTRAT-8006-E015 OTEL scope investigation] --> E016[RHAISTRAT-8006-E016 documentation]\n    E002 --> E016\n    E003[RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 license validation kagenti-operator] --> E016\n    E004 --> E016\n    E006 --> E016\n    E007[RHAISTRAT-8006-E007 license validation kagenti-extensions] --> E016\n    E008 --> E016\n    E009 --> E016\n    E010 --> E016\n    E012 --> E016\n    E013 --> E016\n    E014 --> E016\n```\n\nBranch B (not in the main-plan graph): E001 → RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E017 — if the gap\nanalysis finds functional gaps in the upstream operator, a remediation epic closes them in\nthe upstream `kagenti/*` repos (upstream-first policy) before re-sync to midstream.\n\nCritical path (main plan): E001 → E009 → E010 → E014 → E016 (length 5).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 5 | `repo-onboarding` → `konflux-onboarding` always serial; the Konflux component builds from the midstream fork |\n| E006 → E008 | Rule 5 | Same as above for the kagenti-extensions fork |\n| E001 → E009 | Rule 3 | The upstream gap analysis gates the component controller: if the upstream operator has functional gaps, additional remediation work is required before the deployed operator can meet its acceptance criteria (add_remediation). Konflux onboarding is deliberately NOT gated — the strategy's top risk demands the Konflux submission start immediately, and image building is procedural and independent of functional completeness |\n| E001 → BRANCH-B-E017 | Rule 3 / conditional | Bounded outcome (functional vs. gaps); the branch epic exists only if gaps are found |\n| E005 → E008 | Rule 3 | The variant decision rewrites the AuthBridge Konflux scope (each variant is a separate Konflux component). Not modeled as branch files: the gated epic exists in every outcome (authbridge-proxy is the committed TP minimum per the HLR), only its scope flexes — additive variants fold into the same onboarding epic or a follow-up |\n| E009 → E010 | Rule 13 | The CSV declares the `KagentiOperator` CRD and component-controller RBAC defined by E009 — a build-against artifact, so serial. Image digests for `RELATED_IMAGE_*` are configuration references (Rule 13 exception): E010 gets a \"pinned digests available\" AC, NOT edges to E004/E008, so packaging runs in parallel with image builds |\n| E009 → E014 | Rule 12/13 | E2E lifecycle tests build against the component controller implementation |\n| E010 → E014 | Rule 13 | Disconnected-install validation requires the CSV `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries |\n| E011 → E013 | Rule 3 | Tab-in-project-view vs. standalone navigation entry rewrites the UI epic's scope and effort (~1 vs ~2 sprints). The BFF epic (E012) is not gated — its API surface (list AgentRuntime 