ulti-arch builds (AMD64 required for TP; arm64 opportunistic) | P2 | E004, E008 (acceptance criteria — incidental to the build work, not separately epics) |\n\nStrategy-level acceptance criteria coverage: AgentRuntime CR discovery/selection, metadata\nsync, degraded conditions (MUST/SHOULD) are upstream runtime behavior explicitly out of\nscope (RHAIRFE-7587/7588) — covered indirectly by E001 (validation) and E014 (E2E). The\nsandbox auto-registration COULD and the DSC cleanup MUST map to E009/E014. Documentation\nMUST maps to E016. All seven proposed Given/When/Then ACs are allocated to E009 (1–3),\nE004 (4), E008 (5), E013 (6), E010+E014 (7).\n\n## Investigation Epics and Gate Handling\n\n| Investigation | Unknown resolved | Gates | Failure impact |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| E001 | Is the upstream kagenti-operator functional (three controllers, agent-card metadata fetch)? Does ClientRegistrationController require Keycloak (can it be disabled for TP)? Is the AgentRuntime CRD stable enough? | E009; branch B remediation | add_remediation — gaps ≤2 sprints are closed upstream (branch B); gaps >2 sprints trigger TP scope reduction (defer MLflowReconciler / ClientRegistrationController) |\n| E005 | Which AuthBridge sidecar variants are needed for TP? | E008 | add_remediation — additional variants add Konflux components to E008's scope |\n| E011 | Dashboard TP depth: agent-list tab vs. standalone navigation entry? | E013 | rewrite — UI surface and effort change |\n| E015 | Is the parent RFE's OTEL trace sink integration MUST in scope for TP? | E016 | rewrite — docs scope changes; if promoted, new implementation epics are added |\n\nThe remaining open questions are handled as acceptance criteria, not Investigations,\nbecause they do not change which epics exist or what they do:\n- Cross-namespace cleanup semantics for user-created AgentRuntime CRs on disable — the NFR\n  already mandates CRD deletion (which cascades); the finalizer design is an E009\n  implementation detail captured as an AC.\n- Keycloak runtime dependency — folded into E001's validation scope (it is a property of\n  the ClientRegistrationController being validated).\n- Minimal image contract format (A2A vs. simpler metadata) — upstream runtime behavior,\n  out of scope for this productization strategy; the contract is *documented* by E016,\n  not decided by it.\n- Sandbox CR interaction (OpenShell) — out of scope (agent runtime behavior).\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Scope tension (non-blocking)**: \"Observability wiring (telemetry auto-configuration)\" is\n  listed In Scope, but Out-of-Scope and the TL;DR exclude the operator's runtime\n  capabilities and the observability stack (deferred to RHAIRFE-7589/7589-adjacent RFEs).\n  The decomposition follows the more specific Out-of-Scope/TL;DR reading; E015 gates the\n  unresolved OTEL trace sink question from the parent RFE.\n- **Docs priority exception applied**: the docs-authoring epic (E016) is P0 because the\n  strategy frontmatter priority is Critical (Critical→P0 per the docs-authoring priority\n  exception), even though documentation ships last. Its incoming edges do not push P0\n  upstream (Rule 11).\n- **Data-quality note**: proposed AC 3 references CRD `agentrimes.agent.kagenti.dev` —\n  likely a typo for `agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev`; epic ACs use the corrected name.\n- **Effort risk**: L at the high end; shifts to XL if E001 finds upstream gaps (modeled as\n  branch B). Konflux pipeline capacity \"Needs submission\" — E002/E006 start immediately so\n  E004/E008 can be submitted without delay (top strategy risk).\n- **Port allocation**: the dashboard BFF port (next available in 8043–8743) must be\n  verified against current assignments at implementation time — captured as an E012\n  acceptance criterion, not a blocking unknown.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable as a formal Tier 1/Tier 2 split — no external dependency with uncertain\ntiming blocks user-visible value (upstream repos exist; Konflux lead time is an internal\nprocess gate). The DAG does encode the strategy's implicit tiering: build-pipeline and\nplatform-integration work (E002–E010) proceeds in parallel with, and is not gated by, the\nupstream functional validation (E001 gates only the controller epic E009 and the\nconditional remediation branch).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46047,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8f127c29ec6db28","agent_id":"a0c907d57189bb80b","session_id":"472adfce-b32d-4a5d-9a9c-9f6a006f8387","uuid":"3cda8e25-c5a7-4dd6-8d2a-439f326209b5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:57:01.067Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006"}
