n142\t| E015 | Is the parent RFE's OTEL trace sink integration MUST in scope for TP? | E016 | rewrite — docs scope changes; if promoted, new implementation epics are added |\n143\t\n144\tThe remaining open questions are handled as acceptance criteria, not Investigations,\n145\tbecause they do not change which epics exist or what they do:\n146\t- Cross-namespace cleanup semantics for user-created AgentRuntime CRs on disable — the NFR\n147\t  already mandates CRD deletion (which cascades); the finalizer design is an E009\n148\t  implementation detail captured as an AC.\n149\t- Keycloak runtime dependency — folded into E001's validation scope (it is a property of\n150\t  the ClientRegistrationController being validated).\n151\t- Minimal image contract format (A2A vs. simpler metadata) — upstream runtime behavior,\n152\t  out of scope for this productization strategy; the contract is *documented* by E016,\n153\t  not decided by it.\n154\t- Sandbox CR interaction (OpenShell) — out of scope (agent runtime behavior).\n155\t\n156\t## Health Warnings\n157\t\n158\t- **Scope tension (non-blocking)**: \"Observability wiring (telemetry auto-configuration)\" is\n159\t  listed In Scope, but Out-of-Scope and the TL;DR exclude the operator's runtime\n160\t  capabilities and the observability stack (deferred to RHAIRFE-7589/7589-adjacent RFEs).\n161\t  The decomposition follows the more specific Out-of-Scope/TL;DR reading; E015 gates the\n162\t  unresolved OTEL trace sink question from the parent RFE.\n163\t- **Docs priority exception applied**: the docs-authoring epic (E016) is P0 because the\n164\t  strategy frontmatter priority is Critical (Critical→P0 per the docs-authoring priority\n165\t  exception), even though documentation ships last. Its incoming edges do not push P0\n166\t  upstream (Rule 11).\n167\t- **Data-quality note**: proposed AC 3 references CRD `agentrimes.agent.kagenti.dev` —\n168\t  likely a typo for `agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev`; epic ACs use the corrected n