{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-909c94f8d767baba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E009\n3\ttitle: KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: add_remediation\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the upstream gap analysis finds functional gaps, close them\n15\t    in the upstream kagenti repos before this component's acceptance criteria can\n16\t    pass; if gaps exceed ~2 sprints, reduce TP scope (defer MLflowReconciler / ClientRegistrationController)\n17\t    instead.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tRegisters the kagenti-operator as a new standard component in the rhods-operator component registry, so it can be enabled and disabled through the DataScienceCluster CR like every other platform component. Follows the established pattern of the existing component controllers.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Define a new `KagentiOperator` component CRD in the `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group, following the pattern of `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, `FeastOperator`, and the other component CRDs.\n44\t- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize, releases, kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect); register it in `internal/controller/components/registry/`.\n45\t- Extend the DataScienceCluster CR schema with the kagenti-operator component field; default to `Removed` (Tech Preview opt-in).\n46\t- Implement the `managementState` lifecycle: `Managed` deploys the operator (Deployment, CRDs, RBAC, mutating webhook configuration) into `redhat-ods-applications`; `Removed` deletes all operator-managed resources — controller Deployment, all RBAC (ClusterRoles, ClusterRoleBindings, Roles, RoleBindings), the AgentRuntime CRD, the mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources in `redhat-ods-applications` — following the platform garbage-collection pattern (explicit finalizer enumerating owned resources).\n47\t- Integrate kustomize manifests: pull upstream manifests from the midstream fork at pinned commits via `get_all_manifests.sh`, store under `prefetched-manifests/kagenti-operator/`, and apply RHOAI-specific overlays (namespace, image references, RBAC adjustments).\n48\t- Decide and document the handling of user-created AgentRuntime CRs in other namespaces when the component is disabled (CRD deletion cascades cluster-wide; finalizer behavior must be defined and tested).\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with the kagenti-operator component `managementState: Managed`, when the DSC controller reconciles, then the kagenti-operator Deployment is created in `redhat-ods-applications` with the Konflux-built image, measured by `kubectl get deployment -n redhat-ods-applications -l app=kagenti-operator` returning a Ready deployment.\n53\t- Given the component is `Managed`, when a user creates an AgentRuntime CR referencing an existing Deployment, then the operator applies the `kagenti.io/type: agent` label to the target workload, measured by the label being present on the Deployment.\n54\t- Given the component is changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the controller reconciles, then all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration) are deleted, measured by the Deployment query returning no results and `kubectl get crd agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev` returning \"not found\".\n55\t- The component defaults to `Removed` (disabled) so existing clusters are unaffected by RHOAI upgrade.\n56\t- No RBAC conflicts with other platform operators running in `redhat-ods-applications`.\n57\t- Cleanup behavior for user-created AgentRuntime CRs on disable is defined, implemented, and covered by tests.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- P0: Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard component controller pattern with `managementState: Managed/Removed`.\n62\t- P0: Resource cleanup on `managementState: Removed`.\n63\t- P0: Tech Preview maturity with explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC).\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db2e01fbcd3d520","agent_id":"ae9fc036270642f9d","session_id":"472adfce-b32d-4a5d-9a9c-9f6a006f8387","uuid":"f2532cd8-23d9-466a-8da1-cdeda9800d5c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:05:58.979Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-909c94f8d767baba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
