prints of work, escalate for TP scope reduction instead (e.g., defer MLflowReconciler or ClientRegistrationController) rather than expanding the effort to XL.\n44\t- Re-sync the midstream forks with the remediated upstream code so downstream builds pick it up.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- All gaps identified by the analysis are closed upstream, or a documented scope-reduction decision defers specific controllers for TP.\n49\t- Changes land in `kagenti/*` upstream repositories before the midstream pull (upstream-first policy).\n50\t- Midstream forks are re-synced to the remediated commits and the Konflux-built images pick up the fixes.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- P0 upstream-first policy: significant changes go to `kagenti/*` repos before midstream pull.\n55\t- Protects the P0 DSC integration acceptance criteria (the deployed operator must actually function).\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db2e01fbcd3d520","agent_id":"ae9fc036270642f9d","session_id":"472adfce-b32d-4a5d-9a9c-9f6a006f8387","uuid":"d6a9a9fc-7965-475f-8069-fea0fe6d7cb5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:06:08.626Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac9dbb9bb5535768","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
