{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d6774b620057f98","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tscore: 10\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: critical\n8\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n9\t  description: E009 is missing mandated edges from the kagenti-operator onboarding\n10\t    chain. E009 scope pulls upstream manifests from the midstream fork at pinned commits,\n11\t    an artifact E002 establishes and pins (E002 scope explicitly pins the commits\n12\t    the platform integration renders manifests from), yet E009 depends only on E001.\n13\t    Rule 6 (repo-onboarding to general implementation of the onboarded component,\n14\t    always serial, code needs repo), Rule 13 (consuming implementation builds against\n15\t    another epics artifact, serial), Rule 9 (license-validation to general implementation\n16\t    serial), and Rule 20 (chain places general implementation after license-validation)\n17\t    all require E002 -> E009 and E003 -> E009 edges. E009 is the general implementation\n18\t    of the onboarded kagenti-operator component in this plan. Add both edges while\n19\t    preserving E004 parallel with E009 (Rule 10).\n20\t- severity: major\n21\t  criterion: Epic Boundaries\n22\t  description: E009 is clearly oversized. Its scope bundles the KagentiOperator CRD\n23\t    definition, DSC schema extension, controller action pipeline, kustomize manifest\n24\t    integration with RHOAI overlays, and the Removed-state garbage-collection/finalizer\n25\t    lifecycle; the strategy effort estimate assigns 2-3 sprints to exactly this bucket\n26\t    (rhods-operator component controller), exceeding the ~2-week epic guideline, while\n27\t    the comparable Konflux (2-3 sprints, split into E004+E008) and dashboard (1-2\n28\t    sprints, split into E012+E013) buckets were split. Split E009 along natural seams\n29\t    (for example CRD + DSC schema + controller core versus kustomize manifest integration\n30\t    + cleanup lifecycle) or record an explicit sizing justification.\n31\t- severity: minor\n32\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n33\t  description: E005 -> E008 serializes the committed authbridge-proxy Konflux onboarding\n34\t    behind a PM sign-off (E005), in tension with the strategy top-risk mitigation\n35\t    to submit Konflux onboarding requests immediately; authbridge-proxy is the committed\n36\t    TP minimum per the P1 HLR regardless of the variant decision. Consider gating\n37\t    only the extended variant set via an acceptance criterion (as done for image digests\n38\t    on E010) so the proxy onboarding can start in parallel.\n39\t- severity: minor\n40\t  criterion: DAG Coherence\n41\t  description: E012 feature-flag ACs gate UI visibility on the DSC kagenti-operator\n42\t    component state that E009 defines, with no edge or AC making that coupling explicit;\n43\t    the parallelism is acceptable (flag can default-hide), but an AC noting verification\n44\t    against a live Managed/Removed component once E009 lands would make the intended\n45\t    ordering explicit.\n46\terror: null\n47\t---\n48\t## Review Summary\n49\t\n50\tScore: 10/14 — fail\n51\tRecommendation: revise\n52\t\n53\tFive of seven criteria are clean. Two criteria score 0 and trigger the auto-fail rule: DAG Coherence (a critical missing-edge violation of the onboarding-chain construction rules around E009) and Epic Boundaries (one clearly oversized epic, E009). Neither requires rethinking the decomposition's shape — the epic set, triage handling, branch modeling, and traceability are sound; the fixes are localized to E009's inbound edges and its internal split.\n54\t\n55\t## Criterion Details\n56\t\n57\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n58\t\n59\tAll five P0 and three P1 HLRs map to at least one epic in the traceability matrix, and every mapping was verified against the epic files' HLR Traceability sections: Konflux FIPS operator images → E002/E004; DSC