ure-flag UI visibility against a live Managed/Removed kagenti-operator component once the component controller lands (no edge).\n\nNow, about E009's split and the ai-signals: new epic E018 needs an ai-signals file and frontmatter ai_signals. E009's signals may need adjusting? The instructions say for AI scoring issues, don't touch unless flagged — not flagged. For the split, I need to create E018 with its own ai_signals values (new file). E009's signals can mostly stay (maybe adjust existing_foundation etc.? I'll keep E009's as-is where defensible and craft E018's sensibly, e.g., similar to E009's since it's the same codebase pattern: change_specificity 1, pattern_precedent 1 (platform GC pattern), adapter_pattern 1, existing_foundation 1, open_questions -1 (cross-namespace cleanup semantics undefined — actually that's an open design point, so open_questions -1 fits), external_dependency 0, human_process_gates 0, repo_access 0, architecture_claims 1.\n\nNote: ai_implementability and score — instructions say don't update those, pipeline recomputes. But for a NEW epic, frontmatter requires those fields? Let me check the schema. The instructions for scoring issues say don't update ai_implementability/ai_implementability_score because the pipeline recomputes. For a new epic I need to include something — check schema for required fields. I'll include values consistent with the signals and let the pipeline recompute. Let me check the schema.\n\nAlso E009's signals reference \"open_questions: -1 (gated on the gap analysis)\" — still true.\n\nAlso there's the ai-signals rationale files: RHAISTRAT-8006-E009-ai-signals.md needs updating (scope changed), and a new RHAISTRAT-8006-E018-ai-signals.md.\n\nNow let me read the remaining relevant files: strategy, E002, E003, E005, E008, E010, E012, E013, E014, E016, E009-ai-signals, and schemas. Let me batch reads.","signature":"aca8f9607cd64b558010ea3e832bd803"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null