rences, RBAC adjustments).\n- Decide and document the handling of user-created AgentRuntime CRs in other namespaces when the component is disabled (CRD deletion cascades cluster-wide; finalizer behavior must be defined and tested).","new_string":"Registers the kagenti-operator as a new standard component in the rhods-operator component registry, so it can be enabled and disabled through the DataScienceCluster CR like every other platform component. This epic covers the deploy side: the component CRD, the DSC schema extension, the controller core with its action pipeline, and kustomize manifest integration from the midstream fork. The teardown side — the `Removed`-state garbage-collection and finalizer lifecycle — is a separate epic.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define a new `KagentiOperator` component CRD in the `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group, following the pattern of `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, `FeastOperator`, and the other component CRDs.\n- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize, releases, kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect); register it in `internal/controller/components/registry/`.\n- Extend the DataScienceCluster CR schema with the kagenti-operator component field; default to `Removed` (Tech Preview opt-in).\n- Implement the `Managed` state: deploy the operator (Deployment, CRDs, RBAC, mutating webhook configuration) into `redhat-ods-applications`.\n- Integrate kustomize manifests: pull upstream manifests from the midstream fork at pinned commits via `get_all_manifests.sh`, store under `prefetched-manifests/kagenti-operator/`, and apply RHOAI-specific overlays (namespace, image references, RBAC adjustments)."}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41241,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878a4b50fa68aaff","agent_id":"ab480fced7db1da49","session_id":"472adfce-b32d-4a5d-9a9c-9f6a00