untime CRs in other namespaces when the component is disabled: CRD deletion cascades cluster-wide, so the finalizer behavior for user CRs must be defined, implemented, and tested (cross-namespace cleanup semantics).\n- Make cleanup idempotent and re-runnable on reconcile, so a partially deleted state does not block the DSC controller.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the component is changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the controller reconciles, then all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration) are deleted, measured by `kubectl get deployment -n redhat-ods-applications -l app=kagenti-operator` returning no results and `kubectl get crd agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev` returning \"not found\".\n- Given AgentRuntime CRs exist in user namespaces when the component is disabled, when cleanup completes, then no orphaned kagenti resources remain (webhook configurations, CRs, generated resources), measured by verification across multiple namespaces.\n- Cleanup behavior for user-created AgentRuntime CRs on disable is defined, implemented, and covered by tests.\n- The finalizer completes without blocking the DSC controller when target resources are already deleted (idempotent reconcile).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: Resource cleanup on `managementState: Removed` (controller Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration, namespace-scoped resources).\n- Strategy risk mitigation: \"DSC component cleanup leaves orphaned resources\" — explicit finalizer on the component CR enumerating and deleting all owned resources.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47606,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878a4b50fa68aaff","agent_id":"ab480fced7db1da49","session_id":"472adfce-b32d-4a5d-9a9c-9f6a006f8387","uuid":"be02b1b9-df1f-4efd-8522-7759b8cb65ca","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:20:08.838Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revis