{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b35c8a0bfc399631","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 17\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006 ([TP] Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator)\n11\t\n12\tTriage: full decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy spans four\n13\taffected components, three development teams plus QE and Docs, and is estimated at L\n14\t(6–9 sprints). The Staff Engineer Input section contains only template placeholder text —\n15\tno overrides to apply.\n16\t\n17\t## Component Mapping (canonical RHAI components)\n18\t\n19\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Notes |\n20\t| --- | --- | --- |\n21\t| kagenti-operator | Agentic | Not in `.context/rhai-components.txt` verbatim; \"Agentic\" is the closest canonical component for kagenti work |\n22\t| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | Same mapping; distinct repo/image family, kept as separate epics (different repos and work products) despite the shared canonical name |\n23\t| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | Platform operator component-integration work; rhods-operator is the core platform operator |\n24\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Direct match |\n25\t| QE work (no owned component) | QE | E2E / disconnected-install validation |\n26\t| Docs work (no owned component) | Documentation | Installation and enablement documentation |\n27\t\n28\tNew-component detection: no architecture context file exists for kagenti-operator or\n29\tkagenti-extensions → both get the Rule 20 onboarding chain (`repo-onboarding` +\n30\t`license-validation` parallel start → `konflux-onboarding` after repo-onboarding).\n31\tFor kagenti-operator, the rhods-operator platform-integration work (E009 component\n32\tcontroller + E018 cleanup lifecycle) is the general implementation of the onboarded\n33\tcomponent: it renders kustomize manifests from the midstream fork at the commits E002\n34\tpins, so the onboarding-chain edges (E002 → E009, E003 → E009) apply. For\n35\tkagenti-extensions there is no general implementation epic: the strategy explicitly\n36\texcludes the operator's runtime capabilities (registration, discovery, sidecar injection\n37\talready exist upstream); the work is build pipeline and packaging only.\n38\t\n39\t## Epic List\n40\t\n41\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n42\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality (gap analysis) | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Establish opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator midstream fork | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | License validation for kagenti-operator dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P0 |\n46\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Konflux onboarding for kagenti-operator container image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n47\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E005 | Determine AuthBridge sidecar variants required for TP | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n48\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E006 | Establish opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions midstream fork | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n49\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E007 | License validation for kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P1 |\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E008 | Konflux onboarding for AuthBridge sidecar images | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n51\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E009 | KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator (CRD, DSC schema, controller core, kustomize manifest integration) | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E018 | kagenti-operator Removed-state cleanup and finalizer lifecycle | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator 