{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-849c3624ae768b14","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E009\n3\ttitle: KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: add_remediation\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the upstream gap analysis finds functional gaps, close them\n17\t    in the upstream kagenti repos before this component's acceptance criteria can\n18\t    pass; if gaps exceed ~2 sprints, reduce TP scope (defer MLflowReconciler / ClientRegistrationController)\n19\t    instead.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 0\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tRegisters the kagenti-operator as a new standard component in the rhods-operator component registry, so it can be enabled and disabled through the DataScienceCluster CR like every other platform component. This epic covers the deploy side: the component CRD, the DSC schema extension, the controller core with its action pipeline, and kustomize manifest integration from the midstream fork. The teardown side — the `Removed`-state garbage-collection and finalizer lifecycle — is a separate epic.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Define a new `KagentiOperator` component CRD in the `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group, following the pattern of `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, `FeastOperator`, and the other component CRDs.\n46\t- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize, releases, kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect); register it in `internal/controller/components/registry/`.\n47\t- Extend the DataScienceCluster CR schema with the kagenti-operator component field; default to `Removed` (Tech Preview opt-in).\n48\t- Implement the `Managed` state: deploy the operator (Deployment, CRDs, RBAC, mutating webhook configuration) into `redhat-ods-applications`.\n49\t- Integrate kustomize manifests: pull upstream manifests from the midstream fork at pinned commits via `get_all_manifests.sh`, store under `prefetched-manifests/kagenti-operator/`, and apply RHOAI-specific overlays (namespace, image references, RBAC adjustments).\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with the kagenti-operator component `managementState: Managed`, when the DSC controller reconciles, then the kagenti-operator Deployment is created in `redhat-ods-applications` with the Konflux-built image, measured by `kubectl get deployment -n redhat-ods-applications -l app=kagenti-operator` returning a Ready deployment.\n54\t- Given the component is `Managed`, when a user creates an AgentRuntime CR referencing an existing Deployment, then the operator applies the `kagenti.io/type: agent` label to the target workload, measured by the label being present on the Deployment.\n55\t- Kustomize manifests rendered by the controller come from the midstream fork at the pinned commit(s) established by the repo onboarding, with RHOAI-specific overlays applied (namespace, image references, RBAC adjustments).\n56\t- The component defaults to `Removed` (disabled) so existing clusters are unaffected by RHOAI upgrade.\n57\t- No RBAC conflicts with other platform operators running in `redhat-ods-applications`.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- P0: Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard component controller pattern with `managementState: Managed/Removed`.\n62\t- P0: Tech Preview maturity with explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC).\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-814b0d793f85f566","agent_id":"ae34280954210bdd8","session_id":"472adfce-b32d-4a5d-9a9c-9f6a006f8387","uuid":"3d60c113-d742-4838-b7c5-da37970b1248","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:23:10.477Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-849c3624ae768b14","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
