{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dcf21aa64f4ca94","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E018\n3\ttitle: kagenti-operator Removed-state cleanup and finalizer lifecycle\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E009\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: -1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 0\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 4\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# kagenti-operator Removed-state cleanup and finalizer lifecycle\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tImplements the teardown side of the kagenti-operator DSC component lifecycle. When the component's `managementState` transitions to `Removed`, the component controller must delete every operator-managed resource and leave no orphans — including defining the behavior for user-created AgentRuntime CRs outside the component namespace.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Implement the explicit finalizer on the `KagentiOperator` component CR that enumerates and deletes all owned resources, following the platform garbage-collection pattern used by the existing component controllers: the controller Deployment, all RBAC (ClusterRoles, ClusterRoleBindings, Roles, RoleBindings), the AgentRuntime CRD, the mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources (ConfigMaps, Secrets) in `redhat-ods-applications`.\n39\t- Define and document the handling of user-created AgentRuntime CRs in other namespaces when the component is disabled: CRD deletion cascades cluster-wide, so the finalizer behavior for user CRs must be defined, implemented, and tested (cross-namespace cleanup semantics).\n40\t- Make cleanup idempotent and re-runnable on reconcile, so a partially deleted state does not block the DSC controller.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given the component is changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the controller reconciles, then all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration) are deleted, measured by `kubectl get deployment -n redhat-ods-applications -l app=kagenti-operator` returning no results and `kubectl get crd agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev` returning \"not found\".\n45\t- Given AgentRuntime CRs exist in user namespaces when the component is disabled, when cleanup completes, then no orphaned kagenti resources remain (webhook configurations, CRs, generated resources), measured by verification across multiple namespaces.\n46\t- Cleanup behavior for user-created AgentRuntime CRs on disable is defined, implemented, and covered by tests.\n47\t- The finalizer completes without blocking the DSC controller when target resources are already deleted (idempotent reconcile).\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- P0: Resource cleanup on `managementState: Removed` (controller Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration, namespace-scoped resources).\n52\t- Strategy risk mitigation: \"DSC component cleanup leaves orphaned resources\" — explicit finalizer on the component CR enumerating and deleting all owned resources.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-814b0d793f85f566","agent_id":"ae34280954210bdd8","session_id":"472adfce-b32d-4a5d-9a9c-9f6a006f8387","uuid":"d5179768-b1f9-4613-a831-ffc305d69d7d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:23:11.296Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dcf21aa64f4ca94","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
