{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e36fce3315cccdc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E012\n3\ttitle: Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 0\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRegisters a kagenti dashboard plugin backend in the odh-dashboard Module Federation architecture: a new Go BFF sidecar that proxies Kubernetes API requests for AgentRuntime CR management, plus the `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag that gates all agent-related UI.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Implement a new Go BFF container following the pattern of the existing federated modules' backends (gen-ai, maas-ui, and others); it proxies requests to the Kubernetes API for AgentRuntime CR management (list, get status).\n38\t- Run the BFF as a sidecar container in the dashboard pod on a dedicated TLS-encrypted port, with Bearer token authentication consistent with the other BFF sidecars.\n39\t- Allocate the next available port in the 8043–8743 range, verifying against current assignments (8043-model-registry, 8143-gen-ai, 8243-maas, 8343-mlflow, 8443-eval-hub, 8543-automl, 8643-autorag).\n40\t- Add a `disableKagenti` feature flag (or equivalent) to the `OdhDashboardConfig` CR, gated by the DSC component state: when the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in DSC, the dashboard hides all agent-related UI elements.\n41\t- Register the plugin in the federation configuration (path prefix to sidecar port mapping).\n42\t- Build with FIPS-compliant Go compilation consistent with the other dashboard BFF binaries.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- The BFF sidecar runs in the dashboard pod on an allocated port with no collision against existing assignments.\n47\t- The BFF serves AgentRuntime CR list/status data from the Kubernetes API for the user's accessible namespaces, with Bearer token authentication.\n48\t- The feature flag hides all agent-related UI when the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in DSC, and shows it when `Managed`.\n49\t- Feature-flag behavior is verified against a live kagenti-operator DSC component once the component controller lands in rhods-operator: agent-related UI is hidden with the component `Removed` and shown with the component `Managed`. The flag defaults to hiding, so this verification runs after the controller work lands rather than blocking the plugin work on it.\n50\t- Federation registration routes the plugin's path prefix to the new sidecar.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- P1: Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag for agent views.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-814b0d793f85f566","agent_id":"ae34280954210bdd8","session_id":"472adfce-b32d-4a5d-9a9c-9f6a006f8387","uuid":"1a9e816c-ff61-44cc-ab8b-dff4820accdd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:23:18.483Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e36fce3315cccdc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
