en the kagenti-operator component is disabled.\n46\t- Read-only for Tech Preview — full agent management UI is explicitly out of scope.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given the dashboard is deployed with the kagenti plugin enabled (feature flag active), when a user navigates to the agent views section, then the dashboard displays a list of AgentRuntime CRs from the user's accessible namespaces, measured by the dashboard rendering AgentRuntime data retrieved via the BFF API proxy.\n51\t- The implemented surface matches the agreed TP integration depth decision and its UX design.\n52\t- No agent-related UI elements render when the component is disabled via the feature flag.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- P1: Dashboard integration infrastructure: feature flag for agent views (UI side).\n57\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: users can find running agents and see what each agent can do through the console (TP: read-only list and status).\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-814b0d793f85f566","agent_id":"ae34280954210bdd8","session_id":"472adfce-b32d-4a5d-9a9c-9f6a006f8387","uuid":"6358ac34-7bb6-45f5-9435-2b52f02fff26","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:23:19.471Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab97e8598f86c0f2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
